# Quick requests for VS Code REST Client / Rider / Visual Studio.
# The full, commented collection is docs/postman; every endpoint is in Swagger (/swagger).
# baseUrl: the local stack's proxy (http://localhost:8080) or the API itself (http://localhost:5001).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Readiness (database + object storage)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Log in with the seeded SuperAdmin
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@knox.com",
  "password": "Admin@123456"
}

### Current user's profile
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Universities (public; name filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/universities?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10&name=jadara

### Courses of the admin's major
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/by-major/{{me.response.body.majorId}}?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10

### Course contents (signed file URLs; requires sign-in) - replace 1 with a course id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/1/contents
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Direct upload, step 1: ask for a presigned upload URL (PUT the file to "url" with its "headers", then
### create the material with POST /api/courses/{id}/materials { "title": "...", "uploadKey": "<key>" })
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files/material-uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileName": "lecture.mp4",
  "size": 1048576
}

### Refresh the session (refresh tokens are single-use)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}
